 "text": "-->\nBARRY COUNTY, MO GOV| HOME\ntop of page\nSkip to Main Content\nBARRY COUNTY , MISSOURI\nHOME\nCOUNTY OFFICES\nDEPARTMENTS\nEMERGENCY\nREGISTER TO VOTE\nSowing seeds, Growing futures.\nBarry County, Missouri\nWELCOME TO BARRY COUNTY, MO\nHome of Roaring River State Park\nBarry County, nestled in the picturesque landscape of Southwest Missouri, offers a unique blend of natural beauty, history, and community spirit that makes it a notable part of the state. Established in 1835 and named after William Taylor Barry, a prominent lawyer and politician from Kentucky, the county spans an area that showcases rolling hills, lush forests, and clear waters, including parts of the Mark Twain National Forest and the scenic Roaring River State Park, a haven for anglers, campers, and nature lovers.\nLOCAL OFFICES\n14\nCommunities\n791\nSquare Miles\n34,534\nPopulation (2020 Census)\nBARRY COUNTY, MO\nDepartments and Services\nThe Sheriff's Departmen serves the community by enforcing the law, ensuring public safety, and conducting investigations to protect and serve residents.\nBarry County Sheriff's Department\nThe Health Department serves the community by providing essential public health services and resources to promote and protect the well-being of residents.\nBarry County Health Department\nThe Judicial Center serves as the venue for legal proceedings, offering access to justice, legal services, and impartial resolution of disputes for the residents of Barry County, Missouri.\nBarry County Judicial Center\nCOMMUNITIES\nOur Communities Make Our County Great\nCASSVILLE\nEAGLE ROCK\nMONETT\nGOLDEN\nSHELL KNOB\nSELIGMAN\nPURDY\nEXETER\nWASHBURN\nWHEATON\nAAROW POINT\nSELIGMAN\nBUTTERFIELD\nCHAIN-O-LAKES\nEMERALD BEACH\n700 Main Street\nCassville, MO 65625\n(417) 847-2561\nContact Us\nThe county was created in 1835 and Mount Pleasant was selected as the county seat. The first courthouse was built in Mount Pleasant in 1837. The county seat was moved to McDowell in 1839 and then to Cassville in 1845.\nBarry County Courthouse\nThe Barry/Lawrence Regional Library serves nine communities including: Cassville, Eagle Rock, Shell Knob and Monett.\nBarry/Lawrence Regional Library\nThe 911 Center serves as the vital emergency communication hub, dispatching first responders and providing immediate assistance during emergencies to ensure the safety and well-being of residents.\nE-911 Center\nPrivacy Policy\nBack to Top\n© 2024 Barry County, MO\nHOME\nCOUNTY OFFICES\nDEPARTMENTS\nEMERGENCY\nbottom of page",
